  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to programming, monitoring, evaluation and knowledge sharing in the EU external action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract inherited from multiple actions, related to: Support to programming, monitoring, evaluation and knowledge sharing in the EU external action - This work programme focuses on enhancing the relevance, EU value-added, coherence, effectiveness, efficiency, impact, sustainability and accountability of assistance by means of studies, Result Oriented Monitoring (ROM) and evaluations of policies. It covers projects and programmes financed from the Development Cooperation Instrument (DCI)[1], the European Instrument for Democracy and Human Rights (EIDHR)[2], the Nuclear Safety Co-operation Instrument (NSCI)[3], the Instrument contributing to Stability and Peace (IcSP)[4], the European Development Fund (EDF), Instrument for pre-accession assistance (IPA II and III) and the Neighbourhood, Development and International Cooperation Instrument (NDICI). Activities of this work programme are aimed at assessing the external and internal coherence, including complementarity and synergies between the instruments (also thematic instruments intervening in the regions) and the contribution of the measures to a consistent EU external action.[1] Regulation (EC) No 1905/2006 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 December 2006 establishing a financing instrument for development cooperation [2] Regulation (EU) No 235/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 2014 establishing a financing instrument for democracy and human rights worldwide [3] Council Regulation (Euratom) 2021/948 of 27 May 2021 establishing a European Instrument for International Nuclear Safety Cooperation complementing the Neighbourhood, Development and International Cooperation Instrument &#xbf; Global Europe on the basis of the Treaty establishing the European Atomic Energy Community, and repealing Regulation (Euratom) No 237/2014 [4] Regulation (EU) No 230/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 2014 establishing an instrument contributing to stability and peace</narrative>
  </description>
